%% Treasury Program — disburse_routine flow (batched payroll-style disbursement)
%% Source: treasury-program-design.md §2 (Disbursement flow), §3.3 (OperationsAccount),
%%         §4.4 (instructions), §5 (period rollover), §7 (class enforcement),
%%         §11.1 (Agent Operating Fee, 300 bps)

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Op as Operator (FE)
    participant Tre as Treasury Program
    participant OA as OperationsAccount<br/>[Disbursement]
    participant PA as PolicyAccount
    participant TA as TreasuryAccount<br/>(custody)
    participant Ag as AgentAccount.receiving_address
    participant PFA as ProtocolFeeAccount

    Note over Op: Operator clicks "Run Disbursement".<br/>FE batches N due agents into 1 tx<br/>(N × disburse_routine ix), signed by Disbursement Wallet.

    rect rgb(35, 50, 70)
    Note over Tre,PFA: Per-agent ix (× N in same atomic tx)

    Op->>+Tre: disburse_routine(amount, dest, asset)

    Tre->>OA: load + validate
    Note over OA: signer == OA.signer?<br/>disburse_routine ∈ action_whitelist?<br/>¬revoked? ¬expired?<br/>rate-limit (lazy period reset)?

    Tre->>PA: load + lazy period rollover
    Note over PA: if month ≠ current_period_anchor:<br/>  reset routine_spent_this_period<br/>asset ∈ accepted_assets?

    Note over Tre: fee = amount × agent_operating_fee_bps / 10_000<br/>(dest is AgentAccount.receiving_address<br/>under same company → Agent Operating Fee applies)

    Tre->>PA: require routine_spent + amount + fee ≤ routine_budget<br/>routine_spent_this_period[asset] += (amount + fee)

    Tre->>+TA: transfer (amount → Ag)  +  (fee → PFA)
    TA-->>Ag: amount (full, no deduction)
    TA-->>-PFA: fee (3% default)

    Tre-->>-Op: ok
    end

    Note over Op,PFA: ⛓ Batched atomicity: all N succeed, or all revert.<br/>Errors per §8: OperationsRevoked, OperationsExpired,<br/>RateLimitExceeded, DiscriminatorNotWhitelisted,<br/>AssetNotAllowListed, BudgetExceeded, ArithmeticOverflow.
